{
  "schema": "excalidraw-render/webp-icc-exceptions/v1",
  "approval": null,
  "reason": "Color-managed WebP views: the renderer applies the embedded RGB ICC profile with its pinned CMS (moxcms matrix/TRC and LUT evaluation, rounded premultiplication), while the reference draws through Skia/skcms float arithmetic at draw time. The results differ by at most a few channel units on some pixels. On the 9x7 external libwebp vectors, the canonical small-artifact rule turns those rounding differences into failures that a larger image would pass under the geometry/image budget, as the PNG ICC matrices do. Each exception holds its view at the exact observed Pixelmatch count, differing pixels and maximum channel difference (spec section 14.4, small-artifact form).",
  "comparison": "canonical geometry/image against the pinned reference PNG; PDF only for opaque views",
